1
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,392
Ryotsu, Ryotsu,

2
00:00:10,442 --> 00:00:14,440
Just because it's your day off,
sleeping in a place like this!

3
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:19,400
Ryotsu, Ryotsu, Ryotsu!

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,655
Listen, Ryotsu,

5
00:00:20,705 --> 00:00:26,360
the vase I put here is a souvenir for
the foreign guest who's coming next time.

6
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:29,440
Whatever you do, don't break it. Got it?

7
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:30,820
I'm done for.

8
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:33,120
What a hopeless guy.

9
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:41,280
What? It's Mom...

10
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:45,720
A vase?
Why would I have something like that?

11
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:48,420
As if there'd be a vase at the police box!

12
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:51,760
There's something suitable here.

13
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:55,540
Alright, alright,
I'll bring it over right now.

14
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:56,840
Just wait.

15
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:07,180
When you watch TV, keep the room
bright and sit back a bit, okay?

16
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:55,960
Anyone with no work, come to me.

17
00:01:55,960 --> 00:02:00,600
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

18
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,600
Look, it's on fire!

19
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:08,020
Akaneru too.

20
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:14,320
It'll all work out eventually.

21
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,600
You understand, right?

22
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,580
I know, I know.

23
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:23,500
Once you get it,
just keep quiet and follow me.

24
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:40,060
Tonight's a live broadcast.

25
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:47,640
The vase?

26
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,340
Yeah, it was in the back room.

27
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:53,280
Ryo-chan, do you know where
the camellia-patterned one is?

28
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:55,300
Now that you mention it...

29
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:57,440
Do you have an idea where it is?

30
00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:01,160
My mom said she wanted a vase, so

31
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:05,720
I figured that grubby pot would suit our run-down shack,
so I took it.

32
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:07,780
What about the pot?

33
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:11,360
That's the Chief's precious pot, you know.

34
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:16,220
The Chief came by earlier and made
a huge fuss that the pot was missing.

35
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:19,560
Apparently it's a gift for a foreign guest.

36
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:21,940
That's bad.

37
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:25,500
Alright,
I'll run to Asakusa and grab it right away.

38
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:27,880
If the Chief shows up,
cover for me well, will you?

39
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:40,280
What's with this crowd?

40
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,060
Did a thief break in or something?

41
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,980
Coming through, excuse me.

42
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:45,840
What are we supposed to do now?

43
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,800
Dad, what happened?

44
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,860
Are you alive?

45
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,340
What do you want?

46
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:55,400
What do I want? What do you mean?

47
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,160
Who the hell are you?

48
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:57,940
Isn't it obvious?

49
00:03:57,940 --> 00:03:59,280
I live in this house.

50
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:03,140
Dad, what's wrong?

51
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:04,840
Well, you see...

52
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:07,580
Could it be Fukada from over there?

53
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:11,240
No, the character's name
in this drama is Shizuka.

54
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:13,180
Drama?

55
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:16,740
Director, was there a line like this?

56
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:18,720
What is it, Murata?

57
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:21,700
This police officer suddenly barged in...

58
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:25,560
What do you mean, drama?

59
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,000
Idiot!

60
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:29,780
A puppet drama set in the old downtown.

61
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:31,640
Don't you know?

62
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:35,080
No, Director,
it's today's special broadcast.

63
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:37,840
Even so, a true fan should know!

64
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:48,420
They've been using my
house to film a TV drama?

65
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:49,054
Yes,

66
00:04:49,104 --> 00:04:53,300
it's about a stubborn, old-school tsukudani
shop owner downtown and his daughter.

67
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,380
This drama is going to be a hit.

68
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:57,840
After all, with Akiko Fukada
at the peak of her popularity

69
00:04:57,840 --> 00:05:00,780
and Kazumasa Murata's mature charm in the lead roles,
it's bound to be.

70
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:04,300
Isn't that actress Kiriko Koizumi?

71
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,760
And over here are Aoeda and Seiwa.

72
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:09,720
That cat is the one
from the commercials too.

73
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:20,100
A famous cat's attitude is naturally huge.

74
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:23,100
Its fee is higher than our salaries,
you know.

75
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:27,880
Even so, with this many people in this small room,
is it all right?

76
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:30,420
We're in rehearsal right now.

77
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:33,820
Tonight at 7,
for the station's 35th anniversary,

78
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:36,520
there's a two-hour live broadcast special.

79
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,980
So what happened to the old folks?

80
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:43,340
Surely they weren't kicked out in
just the clothes on their backs...

81
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:44,980
No, not at all.

82
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:48,260
We booked a top-class hotel in central Tokyo,
and they're over there.

83
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,520
A hotel?

84
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:51,140
Yes, Asakusa.

85
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:54,900
The Beauty Hotel's special suite?

86
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:57,620
Huh?

87
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:58,740
Aaaaaah!

88
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:01,340
R-here it is!

89
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:04,320
Wow, this is amazing!

90
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:11,000
Just as expected of the special suite!

91
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:12,160
Kankichi.

92
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:14,680
Is something wrong?

93
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:17,580
Why are you standing right in
front of the door like this?

94
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,920
Well, it's all so over the
top that I can't settle down.

95
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:22,560
Hehehe.

96
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:26,120
What are you doing using only the
four-and-a-half-mat room of the special suite?

97
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,660
Honestly, you're so stingy-minded.

98
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:33,680
Mom, you don't need to do
laundry or anything like that.

99
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:36,480
You don't need to wipe there.

100
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,940
Is it really fine to leave
everything to others like that?

101
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:42,540
It's fine.
That's what they charge the high rates for.

102
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:45,080
What about meals?

103
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:49,480
I suppose the hotel provides three meals a day,
morning, noon, and night.

104
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,260
Sorry to keep you waiting.

105
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:59,400
Lunch is this lavish?

106
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,980
Please take your time.

107
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:04,600
I'm terribly sorry.

108
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,680
Thank you for your hard work.

109
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:09,120
There's no need to apologize.

110
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:12,300
When they're in suits,
I can't help getting nervous.

111
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:16,700
Still, can old folks like us
possibly finish such a lavish meal?

112
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:20,300
We'll leave most of it.
I'm bad with Western food.

113
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:24,660
Just using knives and
forks gives me a headache.

114
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:27,700
I really want some Japanese food.

115
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,740
Then how about we order some sushi?

116
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:31,400
Sushi?

117
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:34,180
There's room service, you know.

118
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:37,180
Wow, it's terribly expensive.

119
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:38,880
It's a hotel, so it can't be helped.

120
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:43,160
Room service?
Ten orders of the premium sushi, please.

121
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,280
What a big splurge!

122
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:46,860
What did you just say?

123
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:48,920
Don't go doing something that'll
bring divine punishment down on you.

124
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:54,030
Don't panic, how undignified. Anyway,
the TV station is paying for everything.

125
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:57,600
No matter how much we eat,
we don't have to pay a single penny.

126
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,420
R-really?

127
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:02,786
Yeah, it's not like it's
coming out of our own pockets.

128
00:08:02,836 --> 00:08:03,820
Don't worry.

129
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:06,660
But there's no way the three
of us can finish all this.

130
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,660
True. Should we invite Gen-san
and the others next door?

131
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:14,040
Yeah, good idea. The suite is big,
and the more people, the livelier it'll be.

132
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:16,800
Then let's invite the
women's association folks too.

133
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:20,620
Okay, then let's add more
sushi while we're at it.

134
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:22,680
Let's also order some good sashimi and sake.

135
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:37,140
I'll sing number 18,
"Katsushika Rhapsody." Tears floating, aiming for the sunset in the sky.

136
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:45,320
Eeeeeeh! Iiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiii!

137
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:50,220
We're getting all this luxury for free,
so it's fine to stay together, right?

138
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:55,920
I brought sushi back as a souvenir for you!

139
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:02,080
What about the sushi?

140
00:09:03,180 --> 00:09:06,760
Chief, with that scary face again.

141
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:10,420
Look, it's sushi! Sushi!

142
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:15,300
What do you think you're doing,
drinking sake on duty?

143
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:19,220
Sorry, Ryo-chan, I couldn't cover it up.

144
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:21,860
So, what happened to the pot?

145
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:23,000
The pot.

146
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:29,580
I hear you took the pot you left here.

147
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:35,360
That's right.
I went to my mom's place for it.

148
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:36,920
You forgot about it?

149
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:39,620
Idiot!

150
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:45,360
That pot was supposed to be
given to a guest from overseas.

151
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:48,420
I'm flying out tonight,
so go get it right away.

152
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:51,760
You know what happens if
you're not back by nine.

153
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:57,120
I was so caught up in location shoots
and everything that I completely forgot.

154
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,580
Hurry, hurry!

155
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:13,860
Five seconds to air.

156
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:14,960
4

157
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:16,000
3

158
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:16,980
2

159
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:17,920
1

160
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:19,660
Meow.

161
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:31,300
35th Anniversary Special, Berabōbe!

162
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:32,920
Tonight it's live.

163
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:37,000
It's starting, it's starting!

164
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,300
Mom, it's starting!

165
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:41,500
They're on, they're on!

166
00:10:41,950 --> 00:10:44,300
Dad, our house is on TV!

167
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:46,560
I feel really good.

168
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:47,260
Really, it is.

169
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:49,120
In a word.

170
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:52,620
What, you've got someone you like?

171
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:56,740
Honestly, these days young guys like that

172
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:58,980
dye their hair brown and wear earrings.

173
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,700
They're all skinny like Abenbo,
the whole lot of them.

174
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:04,220
Can a guy like that
even make tsukudani, nya?

175
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:07,820
Dad, you don't have to jump
to conclusions like that.

176
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:11,920
Yeah, Dad,
your thinking is so old-fashioned.

177
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:15,000
You can't judge people
by their appearance alone.

178
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:15,560
Nyaa.

179
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:18,360
Shut up, kid and cat.

180
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:21,060
So what kind of guy is he?

181
00:11:23,300 --> 00:11:24,760
He's out front right now.

182
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:25,640
What?

183
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:32,300
Sis, we'd better hurry,

184
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:33,440
Oops, sorry about that.

185
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,760
Tadashi-san, Dad.

186
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:43,040
R-Ryo-san...

187
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,680
Am I imagining things?

188
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:49,060
He looks just like Kankichi.

189
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:52,060
That's a mix-up, this one.

190
00:11:52,060 --> 00:11:54,300
Wh-why is that guy on TV?

191
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:56,080
Damn it!

192
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:03,420
Hey there!

193
00:12:04,300 --> 00:12:05,500
Who is that guy?

194
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:07,120
W-what should we do?

195
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:09,720
What do you mean
"what should we do"? There's nothing we can do!

196
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:12,760
It's the 35th anniversary special of the station,
you know!

197
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:16,740
The sponsors are even here watching!

198
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:20,600
We have no choice but to
keep going with improvisation.

199
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,120
W-what?

200
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,500
That guy over there...

201
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:36,160
We've been waiting for you, Tadashi-san.

202
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,900
Come on in, Tadashi-san.

203
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:44,580
Tadashi.

204
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:46,260
Don't be so formal.

205
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:47,320
Don't hold back.

206
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:52,260
Ahhhh, I'm watching!
Just like I said, it's Shara-yaraa!

207
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:56,960
Nah, that's not it.
Even God doesn't have dyed hair.

208
00:12:56,960 --> 00:13:06,240
The two of them are short-legged crew cuts again, the typical Japanese type, Dad.
Oh wow, that's right, isn't it?

209
00:13:11,780 --> 00:13:14,720
Yeah. Tada-san, have a seat

210
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:19,360
So Tadashi-san was a police officer Oh my.

211
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,900
Well, is that so?

212
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:23,480
He even got a detective's certificate once,
you know.

213
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,100
Right, Tadashi-san?

214
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:28,900
No, I get reprimand letters
all year round, though.

215
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:30,620
Tadashi-san, you're at it again.

216
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:33,060
See, he's always like this.

217
00:13:33,060 --> 00:13:34,440
All jokes.

218
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:37,280
Tadashi-san, you're such a funny man.

219
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:39,780
We're in the middle of the live broadcast.

220
00:13:40,180 --> 00:13:42,080
Just do what it says over there.

221
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:47,740
I'm the real deal, I'm the genuine grandpa!

222
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:58,660
Director, what about my part...?

223
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,940
No way! This is my drama debut!

224
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:10,660
Oh no, did he just barge in
during the live broadcast?!

225
00:14:11,685 --> 00:14:14,760
Only 1 hour and 40 minutes left

226
00:14:15,780 --> 00:14:18,320
If we don't deliver that pot by nine...

227
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,120
We have to do something about this.

228
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:26,160
What's wrong, Tadashi-san?

229
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:33,320
Nice to meet you, I'm Tadashi.

230
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,280
Thank you, Tadashi-san.

231
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,540
Kameari Park Police Box, Officer speaking.

232
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:01,540
Terai-san.

233
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:04,320
Ryo-chan's on TV!

234
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:07,120
That's right, turn on the TV!

235
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:09,160
Got it. Okay, then.

236
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:11,200
W-what's going on?

237
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:15,720
I don't know,
but apparently Ryo-chan is on TV right now.

238
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,660
And it's a live broadcast.

239
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,060
What?!

240
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:23,440
And now, the next news.

241
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:23,940
That channel!

242
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:25,360
Bingo!

243
00:15:26,540 --> 00:15:26,860
This is it!

244
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:28,280
F-Father!

245
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:30,300
R-really!

246
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:32,160
What on earth is going on?

247
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,692
To get that pot,

248
00:15:36,742 --> 00:15:39,500
I guess I have to keep acting.

249
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,380
I'll... do it properly...

250
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:46,240
I'll show you the tsukudani
shop while I'm at it!

251
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:50,480
So what's your point?!

252
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:55,040
Please give me that pot!

253
00:15:56,540 --> 00:15:56,940
Ubou!

254
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:58,800
Booo!

255
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:02,040
Well then, that's that!

256
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:05,680
Hold it right there!

257
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:07,540
Tadashi-san, don't go!

258
00:16:07,680 --> 00:16:08,920
Don't you dare apologize!

259
00:16:09,020 --> 00:16:09,460
Meowwww!

260
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:13,100
Let go! All I need is that pot!

261
00:16:13,460 --> 00:16:15,760
Tadashi, it's me you want, not the pot!

262
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:19,380
That's right! You came here to ask Dad for permission to marry,
didn't you!

263
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:22,520
Uh... right, that's right...

264
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:26,960
Damn it, do I still have to keep acting?

265
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:35,360
Sh-shizu... how do you read that?

266
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:38,640
It's "shizuka," you idiot.

267
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:39,900
I-idiot?

268
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:45,480
How dare you say that to my daughter,
you damn fool!

269
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:48,900
Are you Ittetsu Hoshi or something?

270
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:51,580
I'm Yorozuya Shuzo, you damn fool!

271
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:55,740
My old man's name is Ginji, you know!

272
00:16:55,740 --> 00:16:57,360
Shut up, Humer!

273
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,980
I'm right, aren't I?

274
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:01,020
W-was I?

275
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,800
Who cares about that?

276
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:03,580
Dumbass!

277
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:05,400
Now, now, you two.

278
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:07,300
Yeah, calm down, both of you.

279
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:08,080
Please.

280
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:09,120
Meow~

281
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:13,360
Commercial break? Perfect, now's our chance!

282
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,900
That's a good one.

283
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:18,940
Can't see a damn thing in this pot.

284
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:21,720
Found it.

285
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:24,780
What would you do?

286
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,340
A flashlight?

287
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:29,560
But that's a problem.

288
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:32,100
The batteries could die,
you know, that happens a lot.

289
00:17:38,260 --> 00:17:42,560
Even then, with these Tōdai-brand candles,
you'll be totally covered.

290
00:18:12,580 --> 00:18:14,360
I won't give my daughter
to the likes of you!

291
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:16,300
Father.

292
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:19,340
No matter what you say, it's a no.

293
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:24,840
Tadashi-san.

294
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:29,120
It's you, Tadashi-san.

295
00:18:29,120 --> 00:18:30,680
I see.

296
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,180
What is it, Kiriko-san?

297
00:18:32,180 --> 00:18:33,840
It's not Kiriko, it's Matsuko.

298
00:18:34,340 --> 00:18:36,140
Was it? Right...

299
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:37,660
Well, it's not like that, you know.

300
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:39,920
If you're a man, say something!

301
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:42,720
Yeah, go on, tell Dad straight!

302
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,300
I won't leave until you give her to me.

303
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:52,140
You damn fool, I won't give you my daughter!

304
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:54,400
Forget the daughter,
it's the pot that matters.

305
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:58,140
Dad, why don't you stop being so
stubborn and at least hear him out?

306
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:02,720
Yes, if you sincerely ask him,
he's sure to understand.

307
00:19:03,740 --> 00:19:06,320
I'm in trouble if I don't have that pot.

308
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:09,680
The chief yells at me,
and I have to write reports.

309
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:11,480
Hey, please.

310
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:17,780
I don't want anything else, no matter what.

311
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:19,300
I want that pot.

312
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:21,440
No way, I'm not giving you my daughter.

313
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:23,140
I said, it's the pot.

314
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:27,620
Give me the pot.

315
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:29,900
That's really convincing, isn't it?

316
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:32,260
But it's already eight o'clock.

317
00:19:32,700 --> 00:19:36,160
That idiot! Hurry up,
or the plane will leave without us!

318
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,720
If you really want my daughter,

319
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:40,960
then go ahead and take her by force.

320
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:42,880
Don't be so dramatic.

321
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,640
If you're a man, you take her.

322
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:49,940
Hey, we can't just dawdle around!

323
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:52,220
Dad!

324
00:19:52,740 --> 00:19:53,380
Hey,

325
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:55,560
Here, hand it over, then...

326
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:56,020
Here,

327
00:19:56,020 --> 00:19:57,240
Shizuko!

328
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:57,940
Yes.

329
00:19:57,940 --> 00:19:59,440
If we don't hurry with this,

330
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,140
Oh.

331
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:01,280
Stop this!

332
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,020
Ugh.

333
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,720
If you do something like
that and drop the pot...

334
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:07,540
Dad!

335
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:09,060
Here, pass it, hold it, come on!

336
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:11,220
Hang in there, Taxi!

337
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:12,420
Don't you give up!

338
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:18,620
Please, Tower!

339
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:22,820
For a cat, you're way too clever!

340
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:25,100
Come here!

341
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:29,740
Yes! I won't hand it over to anyone now!

342
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:32,340
I won't let you get away!

343
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:39,240
No, don't! Don't go!

344
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:43,240
Hey! Let go!
You're not getting anywhere at all!

345
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:47,040
Ugh, damn it! Not the bicycle! Chase it!

346
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:50,800
I'm not giving you the rice ball!

347
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:51,360
Just so you know!

348
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:52,460
Mom, Dad!

349
00:20:52,860 --> 00:20:58,620
Damn! How persistent!

350
00:20:59,740 --> 00:21:01,040
Mom, Dad!

351
00:21:03,940 --> 00:21:05,580
We have to hurry!

352
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:08,140
No way! Yōji-no-Tono!

353
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:13,440
Super express all the way to Hassō!

354
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:18,500
Put your helmet on or I'll write you a ticket.
Happy now? Hurry up and go.

355
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:20,140
Alright, leave it to me!

356
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:33,060
Things have taken a pretty outrageous turn,
haven't they?

357
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:36,480
That's damn stubborn of him!

358
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:41,080
Still, though...

359
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:43,940
I won't allow you to marry my daughter,
you hear me?

360
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:46,280
Don't say things like that, old man.

361
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:48,180
Dad's just stubborn, you know that.

362
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:49,480
Go bring it here!

363
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:51,600
Hang in there, I'll take a shortcut!

364
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:55,500
Give that to me!

365
00:21:55,960 --> 00:21:59,800
I can't let this live broadcast end halfway through,
not even if I die!

366
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:02,400
What a persistent bastard!

367
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:11,420
Damn it!

368
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:12,880
Oh no,

369
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:15,500
what do we do?

370
00:22:16,260 --> 00:22:16,740
That's it!

371
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:20,660
Hang on!

372
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:28,680
Officer, you're causing trouble.
We're closing up shop already.

373
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:29,780
Found it!

374
00:22:30,180 --> 00:22:31,880
Old man, I'll take this!

375
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:34,400
Alright, this is the last one.

376
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:36,900
That'll be 2,000 yen then.

377
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:40,940
Chief, sorry to keep you waiting!

378
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:46,040
Yes, we still made it in time, right!

379
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:50,940
What's going on with that?

380
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:52,600
Senpai

381
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:55,760
Listen, Ryo-chan, I saw everything.

382
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:58,700
It's a live broadcast.

383
00:22:58,700 --> 00:23:03,560
Your dropping the pot and buying the fake one,
it's all on camera.

384
00:23:03,560 --> 00:23:12,420


385
00:23:12,420 --> 00:23:14,840
I won't do it, please forgive me, I'm sorry!

386
00:23:15,310 --> 00:23:18,480
Confessing your crime on your
own and turning yourself in!

387
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:19,700
That's admirable, Tadashi.

388
00:23:19,700 --> 00:23:22,100
You're a real man, I really admire you.

389
00:23:25,220 --> 00:23:28,260
When you come out after
properly atoning for your crime,

390
00:23:28,260 --> 00:23:31,120
I'll give my blessing to
your marriage with Shizuka.

391
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:32,760
Thank you, Father.

392
00:23:32,760 --> 00:23:34,220
Just as expected of you, Father.

393
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:38,860
I don't really know what's going on,
but it's moving.

394
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:43,120
Kankichi, well done, well done!

395
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:47,520
Kankichi,
make sure you properly atone for your crime!

396
00:23:57,800 --> 00:24:01,000
That's ridiculous!

397
00:24:19,880 --> 00:24:24,460
to those who gamble foolishly on their looks

398
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:27,400
I probably don't want to become that

399
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:32,000
if you're dawdling at the street corner

400
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,340
the moon has run away

401
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:37,900
because now isn't everything

402
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:42,560
don't push yourself too hard

403
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:46,300
even if you tell a little
lie or cheat a little

404
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:50,460
sometimes, while helping someone

405
00:24:50,460 --> 00:24:52,460
Baby, do you know me?

406
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:56,680
facing tomorrow with a nice spirit

407
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:01,820
Don't get lazy, just do what needs doing.

408
00:25:01,820 --> 00:25:04,300
with a cute spirit.

409
00:25:05,060 --> 00:25:07,700
What's hard to see

410
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:11,480
is only because I want it to look that way.

411
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:15,560
Rather than fixing appearances,

412
00:25:29,380 --> 00:25:31,420
Damn, that crazy professor's back again!

413
00:25:31,420 --> 00:25:34,600
What, biotechnology as a
countermeasure for the food crisis?

414
00:25:34,600 --> 00:25:37,260
Whoa, what are these giant shrimp and crabs?

415
00:25:37,260 --> 00:25:39,040
If something like this gets loose...

416
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:42,580
We were just saying it'd be a disaster,
and it's already escaping!

417
00:25:43,220 --> 00:25:47,140
Next time: The invasion of giant bio-creatures,
shrimp, crabs, and squid!

418
00:25:47,520 --> 00:25:48,060
See you next time!

